MacSW @RELEASE@ for SOLIDWORKS 2026 SP4.1
Read this before you open MacSW.

MacSW installs and runs the Windows version of SOLIDWORKS 2026 on an Apple Silicon Mac. It is
based on MacSW by YJBeetle. It is not an official MacSW release, and it is not made or supported
by Dassault Systemes.


INSTALL
-------

1. Get the app. Open the team's Box folder MacSW/releases. Copy @DMG@ to Downloads.
2. Install it. Open the DMG. Drag MacSW onto Applications.
3. Open it. Double-click MacSW in Applications. The first time only, macOS blocks it.
   Do the steps in "FIRST OPEN" below.
4. Confirm the media. MacSW checks the Mac. Click Continue. MacSW then looks for the team config
   and the SOLIDWORKS media in Downloads and in Box. macOS asks whether MacSW may open these
   folders: click Allow. MacSW shows "SOLIDWORKS 2026 SP4.1, found in your Box team folder".
5. Enter the access key. Type or paste the team serial once. Click Install. Leave the Mac on
   charge. MacSW copies the media, installs everything and shows each step.
6. Done. On the last page, click Install SOLIDWORKS App, then Done.
7. Activate. Start SOLIDWORKS (SOLIDWORKS.app, or Launch SOLIDWORKS in the MacSW menu). In the
   SOLIDWORKS Activation Wizard, click Activate now > Automatically over the internet > your
   e-mail > Finish. Activate once.

Time: about 30 to 90 minutes, mostly waiting. Copying 9 to 20 GB from Box takes 10 minutes to an
hour. The first SOLIDWORKS start is slow once (Rosetta translates the code). Later starts take
about 30 seconds.


FIRST OPEN (step 3)
-------------------

MacSW is signed with the team's own certificate, not with an Apple Developer ID. So the first time,
macOS says "Apple could not verify MacSW is free of malware". On macOS 15 and later,
Control-click > Open no longer gets past this message. Do this:

1. Click Done. Do not click Move to Trash.
2. Open System Settings > Privacy & Security.
3. Scroll down to the message about MacSW. Click Open Anyway.
4. Enter your Mac password. Then click Open.

MacSW then asks one question:

   "MacSW will remove the download flag from its own files so that macOS does not block its
   Wine helpers."

Click Remove Download Flag. MacSW changes nothing else.

The Terminal fast path (optional). Instead of steps 2 and 3 of INSTALL, paste this line into
Terminal and press Return:

   bash "/Volumes/@VOLUME@/install-helper.sh"

The script prints each step before it runs it. It checks the signature of MacSW on this disk
image. Then it asks before it changes anything. On "y" it copies MacSW to /Applications (an old
copy goes to the Trash), removes the macOS download flag from /Applications/MacSW.app only and
opens MacSW. It uses no sudo and changes no setting.


WHAT ELSE CAN COME UP
---------------------

- No Rosetta: macOS asks to install Rosetta, or MacSW says it is missing. Click Install. If no
  dialog appears, run this in Terminal: softwareupdate --install-rosetta
- Box Drive: Box downloads the media on first read, and can say the folder is "online only".
  Wait. Or first right-click the folder > Make Available Offline.
- Privacy prompts: "MacSW would like to access files in your Desktop folder" (and Documents,
  Downloads). Click Allow three times.
- Box and iCloud: a prompt for the Box or iCloud folder, the first time SOLIDWORKS should see it.
  Click Allow.
- Activation: in the wizard, click Activate now > Automatically over the internet > your e-mail >
  Finish. If the wizard does not open, use Help > Licenses > Activate in SOLIDWORKS. A
  "SOLIDWORKS License Agreement" window can also appear at the first start. Read it and answer
  it yourself.
- "No activations left" or a similar message: stop. Tell the admin. Do not retry. Each try can
  use an activation.


AFTER DAY ONE
-------------

- Open files by double-clicking them in Finder, or from File > Open in SOLIDWORKS.
- When the admin publishes a new build, install it like this one. MacSW does not check for
  updates by itself yet.
- If something breaks: MacSW menu > Export Diagnostics. Send the zip to the admin.
- Before you wipe the Mac, sell it or leave the team: in SOLIDWORKS, click Help > Licenses >
  Deactivate.
- Do not upgrade to macOS 28.
- Never put the access key in a chat, an issue, a screenshot or a file you share.


CHECK THE DOWNLOAD (optional)
-----------------------------

SHA256SUMS is next to the DMG in the team folder. In Terminal, go to the folder that holds both
files and run: shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS
The line for @DMG@ must say OK.


LICENSES
--------

The Licenses folder has the licence and notice files of MacSW, Wine, Wine-Mono and the other
parts in MacSW.app, as the build made them. SOURCE.txt says where to get the exact sources of
this build.
